# Two 200-row lists under a 44 px bar, side by side, at 640x400 CSS px
# at 1x. Rows are 40 px: white for row 0, 2, 4 ..., grey for 1, 3, 5 ...
# (nth-child(even) is the second row). A wheel of 120 px (one notch)
# over the left list scrolls it three rows, so its top row is row 3
# (grey); the right list is not scrolled, so its top row is row 0
# (white).
wheel 100 200 0 120
pixel 200 50 #dde1e5        left list, top row: row 3, grey, after the scroll
pixel 520 50 #ffffff        right list, top row: row 0, white, not scrolled
pixel 520 90 #dde1e5        right list, second row: grey
pixel 4 4 #171b1f           the bar
ink 310 46 319 398 #dde1e5  the left list's thumb is drawn at its right edge

# A phone: the lists are 195 px wide each; two notches of wheel (240 px,
# six rows) over the left one. Finger scrolling goes through the same
# Document::scroll_target and scroll_node_by (touch_scroll.rs tests).
at 390x800
wheel 50 300 0 240
pixel 100 50 #ffffff        left list, top row: row 6, white
pixel 100 90 #dde1e5        left list, next row: row 7, grey
pixel 300 90 #dde1e5        right list, second row: grey, not scrolled
